commit d91dcfb4c62df190eb8bfed9370b3a5acb7b95b6

C03: a named folder in a known folder goes whole to the private trash (FILES1603)

«Borra la carpeta CarterTest del escritorio» resolved nothing: the deletion reader admitted only file names and the known-file trash adapter enumerated and moved only files. `_FILE_TRASH_REQUEST` now admits «carpeta», «folder», «directorio» as the noun, and `WindowsKnownFileAdapter.Trash` also finds a directory with that name inside the known folders (same depth and reparse-point rules), moves it whole to the product's private trash, post-reads that it left its place and arrived, and records `isFolder`, its entry count and a digest of its relative entry list instead of a file hash. Files behave as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


